    "h1": "How to Get Featured in Digital Journal",
    "title": "How to Get Featured in Digital Journal | DNA PR",
    "description": "Digital Journal covers tech, business and innovation. What it is, what a feature includes, and how to get featured.",
    "body": "<p>If your business is built on technology or a genuinely new approach, Digital Journal is a natural fit.</p>\n<p>Here is what it is and how people get featured.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-digital-journal-is\">What Digital Journal is</h2>\n<p>Digital Journal is a long-running digital publication covering technology, business, innovation and the people behind them. Online only, permanently live, and indexed by search engines.</p>\n<p>Its readership skews toward professionals with genuine interest in how industries are changing — the kind of audience that reads past the headline.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-a-tech-and-innovation-audience-matters\">Why a tech and innovation audience matters</h2>\n<p>Some audiences want the pitch. This one wants the mechanism.</p>\n<p>That is an advantage if your work is genuinely interesting under the hood. Readers here are willing to follow an explanation, which means you can make a real case rather than compressing everything into a slogan. For technical founders, that is a rare amount of room.</p>\n<p>It also means the coverage travels well to investors and partners, who tend to read the same way.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-feature-includes\">What a feature includes</h2>\n<p>A solo, dedicated article about you and your work, with a headline and angle built around your positioning. Typically photos and links to your website, LinkedIn and socials.</p>\n<p>It publishes permanently and stays indexed, so it keeps working every time someone researches you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-get-featured\">How to get featured</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Pitch directly.</strong> Free and legitimate, dependent on fit and editorial capacity.</li><li><strong>Use a professional feature service.</strong> A team writes it to the publication's standard and places it. Faster and more predictable, which is why most founders choose it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-makes-a-strong-piece\">What makes a strong piece</h2>\n<p>Lead with the idea, not the company.</p>\n<p>The features that land here explain something: how your approach differs, what changed in your industry to make it possible, what you learned building it. A reader should finish knowing something they did not know before, and knowing you were the one who explained it.</p>\n<p>Avoid buzzwords. This audience discounts them automatically.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-expect-from-the-process\">What to expect from the process</h2>\n<p>Share your story, our team drafts the piece, you review with revisions until it is exactly right, and nothing publishes until you approve it. Then it goes live and you get the link to share.</p>\n<p>Any provider who cannot show you the draft first is not one to use.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2>\n<p>Digital Networking Agency works with Digital Journal and a wide network of business and technology publications. We write, edit and place. You keep full editorial control, and nothing goes live without your sign-off.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Who does Digital Journal suit?</h3>\n<p>Technology founders, innovation-led businesses and anyone whose story is more interesting when explained than when announced.</p>\n<h3>Do I need a technical product?</h3>\n<p>No, but you do need a genuine idea. The angle can be a method, a market shift or an approach — it does not have to be software.</p>\n<h3>Can I approve the article before it publishes?</h3>\n<p>Yes. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>",
